export const SAFETY_STRINGS = {
  'Road or scooter accident': '公路或機車事故',
  'By far the most likely serious emergency a traveller faces in this region.': '這是旅行者在本地區面臨的、迄今最可能發生的嚴重緊急情況。',
  'Get out of the traffic lane before anything else. Being hit a second time is a real risk on a fast road, and it is what turns a survivable crash into a fatal one.': '首先離開車道。在快速道路上被二次撞擊是真實的風險，而這正是把本來可以挺過去的事故變成致命事故的原因。',
  'Call the national emergency number. Say the road, the direction of travel and the nearest landmark or kilometre marker — a screenshot of your map pin is the fastest way to answer "where are you?".': '請撥打全國緊急電話。說明道路、行駛方向以及最近的地標或公里標，用地圖標記的截圖回答「您在哪裡？」最快。',
  'Do not move anyone who has hit their head or complains of neck or back pain, unless leaving them is more dangerous than moving them.': '對頭部受過撞擊或主訴頸部、背部疼痛的人，請不要移動，除非留在原地比移動更危險。',
  'Control heavy bleeding with firm, continuous pressure through whatever cloth you have. Keep pressing; do not lift to check.': '用您手頭任何布料持續用力按壓，以控制大出血。請一直按壓，不要抬起來查看。',
  'Go to hospital even if you feel fine. Head injuries and internal bleeding declare themselves hours later, and road rash here infects fast in the heat.': '即使您覺得沒事，也要去醫院。頭部受傷和內出血會在數小時後才顯現，而且這裡的炎熱天氣會讓路面擦傷很快感染。',
  'Get a police report. Without one, most travel insurance and every vehicle claim is disputed. Ask for the report number before you leave.': '取得警方報告。沒有報告，大多數旅行保險和所有車輛索賠都會被拒絕。離開前請索取報告編號。',
  'Photograph everything at the scene: both vehicles, the road, the position, any licence and registration, and the other rider. Photographs settle later arguments that memory cannot.': '拍下現場的一切：兩輛車、道路、車輛位置、任何駕照和行駛證，以及另一位騎手。照片能解決記憶無法解決的日後爭執。',
  'Tell your insurer the same day. Many policies exclude motorcycle injury unless you hold a licence valid for that engine size and were wearing a helmet — know which before you rent, not after you crash.': '當天就告知您的保險公司。許多保單會免責機車受傷，除非您持有適用於該排量的有效駕照並戴了頭盔，請在租車前而不是出事後弄清楚。',
  'Do not hand over your passport as security to a rental shop, a hospital or anyone at the scene. Offer a photocopy or a deposit instead — a withheld passport is the standard lever in a rental dispute.': '不要把護照交給租車店、醫院或現場任何人作抵押。請改為提供復印件或押金，扣留護照是租車糾紛中常見的手段。',
  'Do not agree a cash settlement at the roadside before you know the extent of your own injuries.': '在弄清自己的傷情之前，不要在路邊同意現金和解。',
  'Drink spiking & methanol poisoning': '被下藥與甲醇中毒',
  'Rare but not hypothetical — and methanol poisoning is survivable only if it is recognised early.': '罕見但並非不可能，甲醇中毒只有及早識別才能存活。',
  'Treat sudden severe drunkenness that does not match how much was drunk as an emergency, especially after free shots, mixed spirits or home-made liquor.': '如果突然出現嚴重醉酒，與飲酒量不相符，請視為緊急情況，尤其是在喝了免費烈酒、混合烈酒或自釀酒之後。',
  'Methanol poisoning classically appears 6–30 hours after drinking, not immediately: blurred or snowy vision, severe stomach pain, breathlessness, confusion. Any vision change after drinking spirits is a hospital emergency that night, not in the morning.': '甲醇中毒通常在飲酒後 6 至 30 小時出現，而不是立刻出現：視物模糊或像下雪、嚴重胃痛、呼吸困難、意識混亂。飲用烈酒後出現任何視力變化，都應當晚就去醫院，而不是等到早上。',
  'Get the person to the largest hospital you can reach and say the words "possible methanol poisoning". Treatment exists and works; delay is what kills.': '把此人送往您能到達的最大的醫院，並說出「可能是甲醇中毒」。治療是存在且有效的，致命的是延誤。',
  'If someone is unconscious but breathing, put them on their side so they cannot choke, and stay with them.': '如果有人昏迷但仍有呼吸，請讓其側臥以免窒息，並留在其身邊。',
  'Keep the bottle, the glass or the receipt if you safely can — it helps the hospital and any investigation.': '如果能安全地做到，請保留酒瓶、杯子或收據，這對醫院和任何調查都有幫助。',
  'Report it to the tourist police and to your embassy. Clusters are how these venues get shut.': '請向旅遊警察和您的使館報告。正是因為有這類聚集案例，這些場所才會被關停。',
  'Do not let anyone "sleep it off" alone in a room. Almost every death in a spiking or methanol cluster involves someone left to sleep.': '不要讓任何人獨自在房間里「睡一覺就好」。幾乎每一起下藥或甲醇事件中的死亡，都涉及被留下獨自睡覺的人。',
  'Do not accept drinks from a shared jug or a bucket you did not watch being poured, and do not leave a drink unattended.': '不要接受來自共用酒壺或您沒有親眼看著倒的酒桶的飲品，也不要讓飲品無人看管。',
  'Lost or stolen passport': '護照遺失或被盜',
  'Recoverable, but the order of the steps decides whether it takes two days or two weeks.': '可以補辦，但步驟的順序決定了需要兩天還是兩周。',
  'Report it to the local police and get a written report with a reference number. Every embassy asks for it, and so does your insurer.': '向當地警方報案，並取得帶編號的書面報告。每個使館都會要求提供，您的保險公司也是如此。',
  'Contact your embassy or consulate — the nearest one is usually in Bangkok, Hanoi, Ho Chi Minh City or Phnom Penh, and many countries have none at all in Laos.': '聯絡您的使館或領事館，最近的通常在曼谷、河內、胡志明市或金邊，而在寮國，許多國家根本沒有。',
  'If your visa or entry stamp was in it, immigration will need to reissue the record before you can leave the country. Start that on the same day.': '如果您的簽證或入境章在護照里，移民部門需要先重新簽發該記錄，您才能離開該國。請當天就著手辦理。',
  'Ask for an emergency travel document if you have a flight soon; a full replacement passport takes longer and may have to be issued from a regional hub.': '如果您很快有航班，請申請緊急旅行證件；完整補辦護照需要更長時間，還可能需要由區域中心簽發。',
  'Cancel and replace any cards that went with it, and change the passwords for anything that was unlocked on a stolen phone.': '登出並補辦與護照一起丟失的任何銀行卡，並更改在被盜手機上處於解鎖狀態的所有帳戶的密碼。',
  'Do not leave the country by land while the entry record is unresolved — an unmatched entry stamp turns a lost passport into an immigration problem.': '入境記錄尚未解決時，不要從陸路出境，對不上的入境章會把護照遺失變成移民問題。',
  'Do not rely on the photocopy alone. Keep a photograph of the data page and the entry stamp somewhere you can reach without your phone.': '不要只依賴復印件。請把資料頁和入境章的照片儲存在無需手機就能取到的地方。',
  'Robbery, theft or assault': '搶劫、盜竊或襲擊',
  'Snatch theft from a moving motorbike is the common version, and it injures people because they hold on.': '最常見的是在行駛的機車上搶奪，而且因為受害者緊抓不放而導致受傷。',
  'Let it go. A bag is replaceable; being dragged along a road is how snatch theft causes serious injury and death.': '放手吧。包可以再買，被拖在路上則是搶奪造成重傷和死亡的原因。',
  'If you are hurt, treat that first and go to hospital — the report can be made afterwards.': '如果您受傷了，請先處理傷勢並去醫院，報案可以之後再做。',
  'Report it to the tourist police where there is a tourist police unit; they usually have English speakers and handle traveller cases directly.': '在設有旅遊警察的地方，請向旅遊警察報案；他們通常有會說英語的人員，並直接處理旅行者案件。',
  'Freeze cards immediately and check for transactions — card cloning at ATMs is common in this region.': '立即凍結銀行卡並檢查交易，在這一地區，ATM 上的盜刷克隆很常見。',
  'Get the written police report for your insurer; a verbal report is not enough for a claim.': '為保險公司取得書面警方報告；口頭報案不足以索賠。',
  'Tell your embassy if a passport, a visa or your safety is involved.': '如果涉及護照、簽證或您的人身安全，請告知您的使館。',
  'Do not chase anyone, and do not confront a group.': '不要追趕任何人，也不要與一群人對峙。',
  'Do not carry your only card, your only phone and your passport in the same bag.': '不要把唯一的銀行卡、唯一的手機和護照放在同一個包里。',
  'Arrested or detained': '被逮捕或拘留',
  'Drug offences carry severe penalties across all four countries, including sentences travellers do not expect.': '毒品犯罪在四個國家都會面臨嚴厲處罰，包括旅行者意想不到的刑期。',
  'Ask immediately, clearly and repeatedly to contact your embassy. You are entitled to consular access; the request is what triggers it.': '請立即、清楚且反復要求聯絡您的使館。您有權獲得領事探視，提出要求才會觸發這一程式。',
  'Do not sign anything you cannot read, and say so plainly. Ask for a translated copy and for a lawyer.': '不要簽署您看不懂的任何檔案，並明確說明這一點。請要求提供翻譯件並要求律師。',
  'Stay calm and polite. Argument and raised voices make everything that follows harder.': '保持冷靜和禮貌。爭吵和提高嗓門會讓之後的一切更加困難。',
  'The embassy can supply a list of local lawyers, contact your family and monitor your treatment.': '使館可以提供當地律師名單，聯絡您的家人，並關注您受到的對待。',
  'Arrange money through family or your insurer rather than through anyone who approaches you at the station.': '請通過家人或保險公司安排資金，而不要通過在警察局里主動接近您的任何人。',
  'Do not offer money to a police officer. In a genuine arrest it converts a bad situation into a far worse one.': '不要向警察提供金錢。在真正的逮捕中，這會把糟糕的情況變得更糟。',
  'Do not assume a substance is legal because it is sold openly to tourists — cannabis law in Thailand has changed more than once and differs completely in the other three countries.': '不要因為某種物質向遊客公開出售，就認為它是合法的：泰國的大麻法律已多次變動，而其他三個國家則完全不同。',
  'In trouble in the water': '在水中遇險',
  'Drowning is the second leading cause of traveller death here, and rip currents cause most of it.': '溺水是這裡旅行者死亡的第二大原因，其中大部分由離岸流造成。',
  'Caught in a rip: do not swim against it. Float, signal, and swim parallel to the beach until the pull stops, then come in at an angle.': '被捲入離岸流：不要逆流游。保持漂浮、發出訊號，並平行於海灘游動，直到拉力消失，然後斜向游回岸邊。',
  'Helping someone else: throw them something that floats and call for help. Swimming out to a panicking person is how one drowning becomes two.': '幫助他人：扔給對方可漂浮的東西並呼救。游向驚慌的人，會使一人溺水變成兩人溺水。',
  'Out of the water and not breathing: start chest compressions immediately — hard and fast in the centre of the chest, about twice a second — and send someone for an ambulance.': '已上岸但沒有呼吸：立即開始胸外按壓，在胸部中央用力快速按壓，每秒約兩次，並派人去叫救護車。',
  'Anyone who has been under the water needs hospital assessment even if they seem fine afterwards.': '任何曾沈入水下的人，即使事後看起來沒事，也需要到醫院評估。',
  'For a jellyfish sting, flood the area with vinegar for at least thirty seconds and treat any breathing difficulty as an emergency. Box jellyfish are present in the Gulf of Thailand and around the Cambodian coast.': '被水母蜇傷時，用醋沖洗該區域至少三十秒，並把任何呼吸困難視為緊急情況。泰國灣和柬埔寨海岸一帶有箱形水母。',
  'Do not swim where a red flag is flying, and do not judge a beach by how calm it looks — rips are strongest where the water appears flattest.': '不要在飄著紅旗的地方游泳，也不要憑海灘看起來平靜來判斷，水面看似最平的地方離岸流最強。',
  'Do not drink and swim, and do not swim alone at night.': '不要飲酒後游泳，也不要夜間獨自游泳。',
  'High fever': '高燒',
  'Dengue is the biggest infectious risk to travellers in this region, and it is seasonal rather than rare.': '登革熱是這一地區旅行者面臨的最大傳染病風險，它具有季節性，並不罕見。',
  'Any fever above 38 °C that lasts more than 24 hours needs a doctor and a blood test. Dengue, malaria and typhoid all start looking like flu.': '任何超過 38 °C 並持續超過 24 小時的發燒，都需要看醫生並驗血。登革熱、瘧疾和傷寒起初都像流感。',
  'Take paracetamol for fever and pain — nothing else.': '發燒和疼痛請服用乙醯胺酚，不要服用其他藥物。',
  'Drink steadily. Dehydration is what turns a manageable dengue into an admission.': '要持續補水。脫水會讓可控的登革熱變成需要住院。',
  'Warning signs that mean hospital now, not tomorrow: severe stomach pain, repeated vomiting, bleeding gums or nose, black stools, breathlessness, or a sudden drop in temperature with cold clammy skin.': '意味著應立即而不是明天去醫院的警示症狀：劇烈胃痛、反復嘔吐、牙齦或鼻出血、黑便、呼吸困難，或體溫驟降並伴有皮膚冰冷濕黏。',
  'Malaria is a risk in forested border areas rather than the cities. Tell the doctor exactly where you have been in the last month.': '瘧疾的風險在森林邊境地區，而不是城市。請準確告訴醫生您過去一個月去過哪裡。',
  'Do not take ibuprofen, aspirin or any other anti-inflammatory until dengue has been ruled out — they increase bleeding risk.': '在排除登革熱之前，不要服用布洛芬、阿斯匹靈或任何其他消炎藥，它們會增加出血風險。',
  'Do not buy antimalarials or antibiotics from a small shop; counterfeit medicine is a genuine problem outside established pharmacies.': '不要從小店購買抗瘧藥或抗生素；在正規藥房以外，假藥確實是個問題。',
  'Severe stomach illness': '嚴重的胃腸疾病',
  'Common, usually self-limiting, and occasionally the thing that puts a traveller on a drip.': '常見，通常可自行緩解，偶爾會讓旅行者需要輸液。',
  'Rehydrate with oral rehydration salts, sold in every pharmacy in the region. Water alone does not replace what is being lost.': '用口服補液鹽補水，本地區所有藥店都有售。僅喝水無法補充流失的成分。',
  'Small sips, often, are better tolerated than a glass at a time.': '少量多次飲用，比一次喝一杯更容易耐受。',
  'See a doctor if there is blood in the stool, a fever above 38.5 °C, vomiting that stops you keeping fluids down, or symptoms lasting more than three days.': '如果大便帶血、發燒超過 38.5 °C、嘔吐導致無法保持攝入液體，或症狀持續超過三天，請就醫。',
  'A young child, an older traveller or anyone pregnant should be seen much sooner than that.': '幼兒、年長的旅行者或孕婦應更早就醫。',
  'Do not take a stop-the-symptoms antidiarrhoeal if there is blood or a high fever — it can make the underlying infection worse.': '如果有血便或高燒，不要服用止瀉藥，它可能使潛在的感染惡化。',
  'Flood, storm, earthquake or tsunami': '洪水、風暴、地震或海嘯',
  'The regional hazards are seasonal flooding, tropical storms, and — on the Andaman coast — tsunami.': '本地區的災害有季節性洪水、熱帶風暴，以及在安達曼海岸的海嘯。',
  'Feel a strong earthquake on the coast, or see the sea suddenly draw back? Move inland and uphill immediately and do not wait for an official warning. On the Andaman coast, follow the blue tsunami evacuation signs.': '在海岸感到強烈地震，或看到海水突然退去？請立即向內陸和高處轉移，不要等待官方警報。在安達曼海岸，請跟隨藍色的海嘯疏散標誌。',
  'Flooding: never walk or drive through moving water. Thirty centimetres will float a car and knee-deep flow will take an adult off their feet. Flash floods in the northern gorges rise in minutes.': '洪水：切勿徒步或駕車穿過流動的水。三十釐米的水就能讓汽車浮起，齊膝深的水流就能把成年人衝倒。北部峽谷的山洪幾分鐘內就會上漲。',
  'Storm: get indoors and away from windows, trees and hoardings. Boat services stop for a reason — do not press a captain to sail.': '風暴：請進入室內，遠離窗戶、樹木和廣告牌。船班停運自有原因，不要催促船長開船。',
  'Assume the water is contaminated after any flood, and treat every cut and graze that touched it.': '任何洪水過後，都應假定水已受到污染，並處理每一處接觸過水的割傷和擦傷。',
  'Register with your embassy’s travel service if one is available, so you can be contacted during a large event.': '如有可能，請在您使館的旅行服務中登記，以便在大型事件中能聯絡到您。',
  'Do not rely on mobile coverage during a major event; agree a meeting point with anyone you are travelling with in advance.': '大型事件期間不要依賴手機訊號；請提前與同行的人約定集合地點。',
  'Fire in a hotel or hostel': '飯店或青年旅捨起火',
  'Older guesthouses across the region often have one staircase, barred windows and no working alarm.': '本地區較老的旅館往往只有一條樓梯、有欄桿的窗戶，並且沒有可用的警報器。',
  'Get out and stay out. Do not stop for luggage.': '出去，並且不要再回去。不要停下來拿行李。',
  'Stay low under smoke, and feel a door with the back of your hand before opening it.': '在煙霧中保持低姿，開門前先用手背試一試門的溫度。',
  'If you cannot get out, close the door, block the gap with wet cloth, get to a window and make yourself visible.': '如果出不去，請關上門，用濕布堵住縫隙，走到窗邊並讓人看到您。',
  'Account for everyone you are travelling with at a point away from the building.': '在遠離建築的地方清點所有同行的人。',
  'Do not use a lift. Check where the stairs are on the night you arrive — it takes ten seconds and it is the whole of fire safety in a strange building.': '不要使用電梯。到達的當晚就看一下樓梯在哪裡，這只需十秒鐘，卻是陌生建築里消防安全的全部。',
  'Someone you are travelling with is missing': '與您同行的人失蹤了',
  'Report it to the police immediately. There is no waiting period, and the first hours matter most.': '請立即向警方報案。沒有等待期，最初的幾個小時最關鍵。',
  'Contact your embassy at the same time — they can press a case that a local station may otherwise treat as routine.': '同時聯絡您的使館，他們可以推動一樁當地警局可能當作例行公事處理的案件。',
  'Check the hospitals in the area as well as the police; someone brought in unconscious and without documents may not be identified for a while.': '除了警方之外，還要查看該地區的醫院；被送來時昏迷且沒有證件的人，可能很久都無法確認身分。',
  'Gather a recent photograph, what they were wearing, their phone number and any location-sharing they had switched on.': '收集一張近照、其穿著、其電話號碼，以及其開啓的任何位置共享資訊。',
  'Ask their accommodation, their last known driver or boat operator, and the last place they were seen. Local businesses often know more than a station does.': '詢問其住宿處、最後已知的司機或船夫，以及最後一次被看到的地點。當地商家往往比警局知道得更多。',
  'Do not delay to "give it another day". The advice from every consular service is to report early and stand it down later if it was nothing.': '不要拖延「再等一天」。每個領事部門的建議都是盡早報案，如果沒事再撤銷。',
  'A mental health crisis': '心理健康危機',
  'Long trips, isolation, heat, drink and sleeplessness make this more common on the road than at home.': '長途旅行、孤立、炎熱、飲酒和失眠，使這種情況在旅途中比在家裡更常見。',
  'If someone is at immediate risk of harming themselves, do not leave them alone, and call the national emergency number.': '如果有人面臨立即傷害自己的風險，請不要讓其獨處，並撥打全國緊急電話。',
  'Get to a hospital emergency department; the larger private hospitals in Bangkok, Ho Chi Minh City, Hanoi and Phnom Penh have psychiatric services, most public provincial hospitals do not.': '前往醫院急診科；曼谷、胡志明市、河內和金邊較大的私立醫院設有精神科服務，大多數省級公立醫院沒有。',
  'Remove the immediate means of harm if you can do so safely.': '如果能安全地做到，請移除可能立即造成傷害的物品。',
  'Your travel insurer’s assistance line can arrange a psychiatric referral and, where needed, a medically escorted flight home.': '您的旅行保險公司的援助熱線可以安排精神科轉診，必要時安排有醫護陪同的回國航班。',
  'Your embassy can contact family and help with practical arrangements.': '您的使館可以聯絡家人，並協助處理實際安排。',
  'Local mental health services are limited in Cambodia and Laos in particular; getting to a major city, or home, is often the realistic plan.': '尤其是在柬埔寨和寮國，當地心理健康服務有限；前往大城市或回國往往是現實的方案。',
  'Do not treat "they have been drinking" as an explanation that makes it less urgent.': '不要把「他們喝了酒」當作讓事情不那麼緊急的解釋。',
  'If a traveller dies': '如果有旅行者去世',
  'The hardest page here, written down so nobody has to work it out while grieving.': '這裡最沈重的一頁，寫下來是為了讓沒有人需要在悲痛中自己摸索該怎麼辦。',
  'Contact your embassy or consulate first. Repatriation, local registration of the death and the paperwork all run through them, and they will explain the order of it.': '首先聯絡您的使館或領事館。遺體送返、當地死亡登記和各項檔案都通過他們辦理，他們會解釋先後順序。',
  'Contact the travel insurer. Repatriation of remains is expensive and is the single most valuable thing a policy covers.': '聯絡旅行保險公司。遺體送返費用昂貴，是保單承保的最有價值的一項。',
  'A local death certificate is issued by the authorities where the death occurred; the embassy can advise on getting it recognised at home.': '當地死亡證明由死亡發生地的當局簽發；使館可就如何在國內獲得承認提供建議。',
  'Do not agree to a cremation or a burial before speaking to the embassy and the family — in some countries it cannot be undone or reversed.': '在與使館和家人商量之前，不要同意火化或土葬，在某些國家，這是無法撤銷或逆轉的。',
  'Issue an emergency travel document or a replacement passport.': '簽發緊急旅行證件或補發護照。',
  'Contact your family and help you get money sent to you.': '聯絡您的家人，並幫助您接收匯款。',
  'Visit you and monitor your treatment if you are arrested or detained.': '如果您被逮捕或拘留，探視您並關注您受到的對待。',
  'Give you a list of local lawyers, translators and doctors.': '給您提供當地律師、翻譯和醫生的名單。',
  'Help in a death, a serious accident, or a large-scale emergency.': '協助處理死亡、嚴重事故或大規模緊急事件。',
  'Give you the current official travel and health advice for where you are.': '提供您所在地當前的官方旅行和健康建議。',
  'Get you out of prison, or interfere in a local investigation or court case.': '把您從監獄中救出，或干預當地的調查或法庭案件。',
  'Pay your medical bills, your legal costs or your fare home.': '支付您的醫療費、法律費用或回程機票。',
  'Investigate a crime, or make the police act faster than local law allows.': '調查犯罪，或讓警方比當地法律允許的更快採取行動。',
  'Give you legal or medical advice of its own.': '自行為您提供法律或醫療建議。',
  'Many countries have an embassy in Bangkok, Hanoi and Phnom Penh but none at all in Vientiane — in Laos your nearest consular help is often in Bangkok. Find yours, and save the address and the emergency line, before you need it.': '許多國家在曼谷、河內和金邊設有使館，但在萬象完全沒有，在寮國，您最近的領事協助通常在曼谷。請在需要之前，找到您的使館，並儲存其地址和緊急熱線。',
  '24h emergency': '24 小時急診',
  'Children': '兒童',
  'Maternity': '產科',
  'English / international': '英語 / 國際服務',
  'Major trauma & surgery': '重大創傷與外科',
  'Hyperbaric (dive) chamber': '高壓氧艙（潛水）',
  'Arranges medical evacuation': '安排醫療後送',
  'Not responding, or not breathing normally': '無反應，或呼吸不正常',
  'Allergic reaction & breathing emergencies': '過敏反應與呼吸急症',
  'Bleeding, shock, burns & collapse': '出血、休克、燒傷與昏倒',
  'Heart, stroke & blood sugar': '心臟、中風與血糖',
  'Babies & children — everyday emergencies': '嬰幼兒：常見急症',
  'Snakes, marine life & animal bites': '蛇、海洋生物與動物咬傷',
  'Water, weather & getting help': '水、天氣與獲取幫助',
  'Someone collapses, or will not wake up': '有人昏倒，或叫不醒',
  'Check for a response — speak loudly and gently shake their shoulders (a baby: tap the foot, do not shake).': '檢查有無反應：大聲說話並輕拍其肩膀（嬰兒：拍打腳底，不要搖晃）。',
  'If they respond and are breathing normally: do not move them if you suspect a neck or back injury; otherwise put them in the recovery position (below) and keep checking their breathing.': '如果對方有反應且呼吸正常：若懷疑頸部或背部受傷，請不要移動；否則讓其採取復甦姿勢（見下文），並持續觀察呼吸。',
  'If they do NOT respond: shout for help, and check breathing for up to 10 seconds — look, listen, feel. Noisy, gasping or irregular breathing counts as "not breathing normally".': '如果對方沒有反應：大聲呼救，並檢查呼吸最多 10 秒：看、聽、感覺。有雜音、喘息或不規則的呼吸都算作「呼吸不正常」。',
  'Not breathing, or not breathing normally: call the emergency number on speakerphone (or send someone to) and start CPR immediately — see the adult/child or baby steps below. Do not wait to find a pulse; lay rescuers are not asked to check for one.': '沒有呼吸或呼吸不正常：用免提撥打緊急電話（或讓人去打），並立即開始心肺復蘇，參見下方成人 / 兒童或嬰兒的步驟。不要等著去摸脈搏，非專業施救者不需要檢查脈搏。',
  'Send someone to find an AED (defibrillator) if one might be nearby — large hotels, malls and airports sometimes have one.': '如果附近可能有 AED（去顫器），請讓人去找，大型飯店、商場和機場有時設有。',
  'CPR — adult and child over about 1 year': '心肺復蘇：成人和約 1 歲以上兒童',
  'Lay them on their back on a firm, flat surface.': '讓其仰臥在堅硬平整的表面上。',
  'Heel of one hand on the centre of the chest (lower half of the breastbone); for a child, one or two hands depending on their size.': '一隻手的掌根放在胸部中央（胸骨下半部）；兒童視體型使用一隻或兩只手。',
  'Push hard and fast: adult depth 5–6 cm, child about one-third of the chest’s depth (roughly 5 cm) — both at 100–120 pushes per minute, letting the chest fully rise between pushes.': '用力快速按壓：成人按壓深度 5–6 釐米，兒童約為胸廓深度的三分之一（約 5 釐米），頻率均為每分鐘 100–120 次，每次按壓之間讓胸廓完全回彈。',
  'If trained and willing: 30 pushes, then 2 rescue breaths, repeating (children may be given 15:2 if there are two trained rescuers). If untrained, unwilling, or unable to give breaths: continuous push-only CPR is still far better than nothing.': '如果受過訓練且願意：按壓 30 次，然後人工呼吸 2 次，循環進行（如有兩位受過訓練的施救者，兒童可用 15:2）。如果未受訓練、不願意或無法做人工呼吸：持續只做按壓的心肺復蘇仍遠好於什麼都不做。',
  'Use an AED the moment one arrives and follow its voice prompts — it will not shock unless a shock is needed.': 'AED 一到就立即使用，並遵循其語音提示，只有在需要電擊時它才會電擊。',
  'Keep going until the person starts breathing normally, professional help takes over, or you are physically unable to continue.': '持續進行，直到對方恢復正常呼吸、專業人員接手，或您體力不支無法繼續。',
  'Alone with no phone: with an adult, call first, then start CPR. With a child, current guidance is to give CPR for about one to two minutes first if you truly cannot call and compress at the same time (put the phone on speaker and start compressions the moment you have dialled, if that is possible instead).': '獨自一人且沒有手機：對成人，先打電話，再開始心肺復蘇。對兒童，現行指南是如果確實無法同時打電話和按壓，先做約一到兩分鐘的心肺復蘇（如果可能，改為把手機開免提，撥通後立刻開始按壓）。',
  'A rescuer taught with breaths first (5 initial breaths before compressions, still taught in the UK/Europe for children) and one taught compressions-first (the US/AHA approach) are both following a currently-endorsed method — do not hesitate over which to use.': '先做人工呼吸的施救者（按壓前先做 5 次初始呼吸，英國 / 歐洲對兒童仍這樣教）和先按壓的施救者（美國 / AHA 方法）都遵循目前認可的方法，不要在用哪種上猶豫。',
  'CPR — baby under 1 year': '心肺復蘇：1 歲以下嬰兒',
  'Lay the baby on their back on a firm surface, head in a neutral position (not tilted back).': '讓嬰兒仰臥在堅硬表面上，頭部保持中立位置（不要後仰）。',
  'For rescue breaths, your mouth covers the baby’s mouth AND nose.': '做人工呼吸時，您的嘴要同時蓋住嬰兒的口和鼻。',
  'Compress the lower half of the breastbone, just below the nipple line, using two thumbs wrapped around the chest (preferred where you can manage it) or the heel of one hand if you cannot encircle the chest — two fingers is also still taught in some countries and is not wrong if that is what you learned.': '按壓胸骨下半部，位於乳頭連線正下方，用兩個拇指環繞胸部按壓（如能做到則為首選），如果無法環抱胸部，則用一隻手的掌根，有些國家仍教用兩根手指，如果您學的是這種方法，也沒有錯。',
  'Push at least one-third of the chest’s depth (about 4 cm), 100–120 per minute.': '按壓深度至少為胸廓深度的三分之一（約 4 釐米），每分鐘 100–120 次。',
  '30 compressions to 2 breaths for a single rescuer; 15:2 if there are two trained rescuers.': '單人施救按壓 30 次、人工呼吸 2 次；如有兩位受過訓練的施救者則為 15:2。',
  'Keep going until the baby responds, help takes over, or you cannot continue.': '持續進行，直到嬰兒有反應、專業人員接手，或您無法繼續。',
  'Which hand technique is "correct" is genuinely still shifting between countries as of 2026 — two-thumb encircling is now preferred almost everywhere, but two-finger and heel-of-one-hand are still taught and are not mistakes.': '到 2026 年，哪種手法才是「正確的」在各國之間仍在變化：目前幾乎各地都首選雙拇指環抱法，但雙指法和單手掌根法仍有教授，也不算錯誤。',
  'Choking — adult and child over about 1 year': '噎食：成人和約 1 歲以上兒童',
  'If they can cough, speak or breathe: encourage coughing and do nothing else yet.': '如果對方能咳嗽、說話或呼吸：鼓勵其咳嗽，暫時不要做其他事。',
  'If they cannot cough, speak or breathe: give up to 5 firm blows between the shoulder blades with the heel of your hand.': '如果對方無法咳嗽、說話或呼吸：用手掌根在兩肩胛骨之間用力拍擊最多 5 次。',
  'Not cleared: give up to 5 abdominal thrusts — stand behind them, fist just above the navel, pull sharply inward and upward. (Some countries — Australia and New Zealand — teach chest thrusts instead of abdominal thrusts; both are recognised as effective.)': '未排出：做最多 5 次腹部衝擊，站在其身後，拳頭放在肚臍上方，向內向上猛力拉。（有些國家，如澳大利亞和新西蘭，教的是胸部衝擊而不是腹部衝擊，兩者都被認為有效。）',
  'Keep alternating 5 back blows with 5 thrusts until the object clears or the person becomes unresponsive.': '繼續交替進行 5 次背部拍擊和 5 次衝擊，直到異物排出或對方失去反應。',
  'If they become unresponsive: lower them to the ground and start CPR (above) — look in the mouth each time you open the airway and only remove an object you can actually see.': '如果對方失去反應：讓其平躺到地上並開始心肺復蘇（見上文），每次開啟氣道時都查看口腔，只取出您確實能看到的異物。',
  'Anyone who was given abdominal thrusts should see a doctor afterwards, even once the object is out — they can cause internal injury.': '接受過腹部衝擊的人事後應就醫，即使異物已經排出，因為腹部衝擊可能造成內傷。',
  'Never do a blind finger sweep of the mouth.': '切勿盲目用手指在口中探挖。',
  'Choking — baby under 1 year': '噎食：1 歲以下嬰兒',
  'Lay the baby face down along your forearm or thigh, head lower than their chest, supporting the head and jaw.': '讓嬰兒臉朝下趴在您的前臂或大腿上，頭低於胸部，並托住頭部和下頜。',
  'Give up to 5 firm back blows between the shoulder blades with the heel of your hand, checking between each.': '用手掌根在兩肩胛骨之間用力拍擊最多 5 次，每次之後都檢查。',
  'Not cleared: turn the baby face up (still head-down along your arm/thigh) and give up to 5 chest thrusts on the lower half of the breastbone, just below the nipple line — two fingers, two thumbs, or the heel of one hand are all currently taught; use whichever you know.': '未排出：把嬰兒翻成臉朝上（仍然頭低位，趴在您的手臂 / 大腿上），在胸骨下半部、乳頭連線正下方做最多 5 次胸部衝擊，兩根手指、兩個拇指或單手掌根目前都有教授，用您熟悉的即可。',
  'Keep alternating 5 back blows with 5 chest thrusts.': '繼續交替進行 5 次背部拍擊和 5 次胸部衝擊。',
  'If the baby becomes unresponsive: start baby CPR (above) and get emergency help.': '如果嬰兒失去反應：開始嬰兒心肺復蘇（見上文）並獲取緊急救援。',
  'Never give abdominal thrusts to a baby — real risk of internal injury.': '切勿對嬰兒做腹部衝擊，有造成內傷的實際風險。',
  'Never do a blind finger sweep; only remove an object you can actually see.': '切勿盲目用手指探挖，只取出您確實能看到的異物。',
  'Recovery position': '復甦姿勢',
  'For someone unresponsive but breathing normally, with no reason to suspect CPR or serious bleeding is needed: roll them onto their side and tilt the head back slightly, so the airway stays open and fluid can drain out. Do not put them on their back.': '對於無反應但呼吸正常、且沒有理由懷疑需要心肺復蘇或嚴重出血的人：讓其側臥並稍微後仰頭部，使氣道保持通暢，液體可以流出。不要讓其仰臥。',
  'A baby: do not put them on the floor — hold them face down along your forearm, head supported and tilted a little lower than the body.': '嬰兒：不要放在地板上，讓其臉朝下趴在您的前臂上，托住頭部，並讓頭比身體稍低。',
  'Keep watching their breathing until help arrives. Noisy, irregular or gasping breathing is a sign to treat them as not breathing and start CPR instead.': '在救援到達前持續觀察其呼吸。有雜音、不規則或喘息式呼吸，說明應當視為沒有呼吸並改做心肺復蘇。',
  'A pregnant woman should go on her LEFT side.': '孕婦應取左側臥位。',
  'Drowning': '溺水',
  'Do not swim out to them unless you are trained for water rescue — reach with a pole, branch or rope, or throw something that floats, instead.': '除非受過水上救援訓練，否則不要游向對方，請改用桿子、樹枝或繩子夠到對方，或扔給對方可漂浮的東西。',
  'Once they are out of the water and not breathing normally: open the airway and give a few rescue breaths (guidance ranges from 2 to 5; 5 is now the most common number taught), then continue CPR at the normal ratio (30 compressions to 2 breaths).': '對方出水後如果呼吸不正常：開啟氣道並做幾次人工呼吸（指南從 2 次到 5 次不等，5 次是目前最常教的數字），然後按正常比例（按壓 30 次、人工呼吸 2 次）繼續心肺復蘇。',
  'Untrained, unwilling or unable to give breaths: compression-only CPR is still far better than nothing, but breaths genuinely improve survival after drowning specifically, more than in an ordinary adult cardiac arrest — give them if you can.': '未受訓練、不願意或無法做人工呼吸：只做按壓的心肺復蘇仍遠好於什麼都不做，但人工呼吸確實能提高溺水後的存活率，尤其是比普通成人心臟驟停更明顯，請盡量做。',
  'Vomiting is common during resuscitation — be ready to roll the person onto their side and clear the mouth, then continue.': '復蘇期間常會嘔吐，請做好準備，把對方翻成側臥並清理口腔，然後繼續。',
  'Everyone who was pulled from the water unresponsive, needed rescue breaths or CPR, or has any cough, breathlessness, confusion or drowsiness afterwards must be seen at a hospital, even if they seem to recover — a delayed reaction (secondary drowning) is real.': '所有被從水中救起時無反應、需要人工呼吸或心肺復蘇，或事後出現任何咳嗽、呼吸急促、意識混亂或嗜睡的人，即使看似恢復也必須到醫院檢查，延遲反應（繼發性溺水）是真實存在的。',
  'Recognise anaphylaxis (severe allergic reaction)': '識別過敏性休克（嚴重過敏反應）',
  'Sudden breathing or circulation trouble after a food, sting or medicine: swelling of the tongue or throat, noisy or difficult breathing, a wheeze or persistent cough, a hoarse voice, difficulty swallowing, dizziness or collapse.': '在食用食物、被蜇或服藥後突然出現呼吸或循環問題：舌頭或喉嚨腫脹、呼吸有雜音或困難、喘鳴或持續咳嗽、聲音嘶啞、吞咽困難、頭暈或昏倒。',
  'Often — but not always — with hives or skin swelling. A reaction can be severe with no skin signs at all.': '常伴有蕁麻疹或皮膚腫脹，但並非總是如此。反應可能很嚴重，卻沒有任何皮膚表現。',
  'In babies and young children specifically: sudden pale, floppy or limp, not responding normally.': '尤其是嬰幼兒：突然臉色蒼白、軟綿綿或癱軟、反應不正常。',
  'Anaphylaxis — what to do': '過敏性休克：該怎麼做',
  'If an adrenaline (epinephrine) auto-injector is available, use it AT ONCE into the outer mid-thigh — through clothing is fine.': '如有腎上腺素自動注射器，請立即注射在大腿外側中部，隔著衣服也可以。',
  'Call the emergency number straight away.': '立即撥打緊急電話。',
  'Lie the person flat and raise their legs; if breathing is very hard, let them sit up instead. Someone pregnant should lie on her left side.': '讓對方平躺並抬高雙腿；如果呼吸非常困難，則讓其坐起。孕婦應左側臥。',
  'Do not let them stand or walk, even once they feel better — a sudden drop in blood pressure while upright can be fatal.': '不要讓其站立或走動，即使感覺好轉，直立時血壓驟降可能致命。',
  'No improvement after about 5 minutes and a second auto-injector is available: give the second dose.': '約 5 分鐘後仍無改善且有第二支自動注射器：注射第二劑。',
  'Go to hospital every time, even after a full recovery — symptoms can return hours later (a biphasic reaction).': '每次都要去醫院，即使完全恢復，症狀也可能在數小時後復發（雙相反應）。',
  'If in genuine doubt whether it is anaphylaxis, every source agrees: give the adrenaline. The risk of a dose given when it was not strictly needed is far smaller than the risk of withholding it when it was.': '如果真的拿不准是否為過敏性休克，所有來源都一致認為：注射腎上腺素。在並非嚴格需要時注射一劑的風險，遠小於在需要時不注射的風險。',
  'Anaphylaxis in babies and children': '嬰幼兒過敏性休克',
  'Lay a baby or toddler flat — never hold them upright.': '讓嬰兒或幼兒平躺，切勿竪抱。',
  'Use their own prescribed auto-injector at its prescribed dose the moment anaphylaxis is suspected.': '一旦懷疑過敏性休克，立即按處方劑量使用其本人的處方自動注射器。',
  'Auto-injector doses run roughly: 0.1 mg for about 7.5–15 kg (where that device exists), 0.15 mg from about 7.5–20 kg up to 30 kg depending on country and device, 0.3 mg above about 20–30 kg.': '自動注射器的劑量大致為：約 7.5–15 公斤用 0.1 毫克（該型號存在的情況下），約 7.5–20 公斤至 30 公斤用 0.15 毫克（因國家和器械而異），約 20–30 公斤以上用 0.3 毫克。',
  'Under about 7.5 kg, or any child with no prescribed device: call the emergency number immediately and let paramedics or a doctor decide the dose — do not improvise with a mismatched adult device.': '體重約 7.5 公斤以下，或沒有處方器械的任何兒童：請立即撥打緊急電話，由急救人員或醫生決定劑量，不要隨意使用不匹配的成人器械。',
  'Dosing bands genuinely differ between countries and auto-injector brands — this is not a single fixed number worldwide. Always follow the child’s own prescribed device and plan where one exists.': '各國和各品牌自動注射器的劑量區間確實有差異，全球並沒有統一的固定數值。如有該兒童自己的處方器械和方案，請始終遵循。',
  'Asthma attack': '哮喘發作',
  'Help them sit upright — never lie them down. Stay calm; anxiety worsens breathing.': '幫助其坐直，切勿讓其躺下。保持冷靜，焦慮會加重呼吸困難。',
  'Use the blue/grey reliever inhaler at once, with a spacer if one is available.': '立即使用藍色 / 灰色的緩解型吸入器，如有儲霧罐請配合使用。',
  'They have their own written asthma action plan: follow its dosing exactly.': '如果對方有自己的書面哮喘行動計劃：請嚴格按其劑量執行。',
  'No plan: either recognised approach is safe — 1 puff every 30–60 seconds up to 10 puffs (UK-style), or 4 puffs (one at a time via a spacer, 4 breaths each), wait 4 minutes, then repeat (Australia-style).': '沒有計劃：兩種公認的方法都是安全的：每 30–60 秒吸 1 次，最多 10 次（英國方式），或吸 4 次（通過儲霧罐每次一噴，各呼吸 4 次），等待 4 分鐘後重復（澳大利亞方式）。',
  'Call the emergency number if: there is no inhaler, the inhaler is not helping, lips or fingers turn blue, the person is exhausted or confused, breathing becomes quiet or slow, or symptoms have not resolved after the full first round.': '出現以下情況請撥打緊急電話：沒有吸入器、吸入器無效、嘴唇或手指發紫、對方筋疲力盡或意識混亂、呼吸變得安靜或緩慢，或完成第一輪後症狀仍未緩解。',
  'Severe bleeding': '嚴重出血',
  'Apply firm, continuous direct pressure over the wound with whatever is available — a cloth, clothing, your hand.': '用手邊任何東西（布、衣物、您的手）在傷口上持續用力直接按壓。',
  'Life-threatening limb bleeding not controlled by pressure: apply a tourniquet a few centimetres above the wound — never over a joint — and tighten until the bleeding stops. Note the exact time it went on and do not loosen it.': '按壓無法控制的危及生命的肢體出血：在傷口上方幾釐米處綁止血帶，切勿綁在關節上，並擰緊直到出血停止。記下綁上的確切時間，且不要松開。',
  'A deep wound somewhere a tourniquet cannot go (neck, groin, armpit): pack the wound firmly and press.': '止血帶無法使用的部位（頸部、腹股溝、腋窩）的深部傷口：把傷口緊緊填塞並按壓。',
  'Call the emergency number for any severe bleeding.': '任何嚴重出血都要撥打緊急電話。',
  'A proper manufactured tourniquet is best; sources genuinely disagree on improvising one from a belt or scarf as a last resort — most say it is better than nothing for life-threatening limb bleeding, one major source (Mayo Clinic) advises against it. If a limb is bleeding life-threateningly and nothing manufactured exists, an improvised tourniquet — a firm, wide band tightened with a rigid object — is the safer choice for most authorities.': '專業製造的止血帶最好；對於在萬不得已時用腰帶或圍巾臨時製作的做法，各來源確實存在分歧，大多數認為對危及生命的肢體出血總比什麼都不做強，有一個主要來源（梅奧診所）則建議不要這樣做。如果肢體出血危及生命且沒有專業產品，大多數權威機構認為臨時止血帶，即用硬物擰緊的寬而牢固的帶子，是更安全的選擇。',
  'Shock': '休克',
  'Signs: pale, cold, clammy skin, rapid weak pulse, rapid shallow breathing, confusion or weakness.': '表現：皮膚蒼白、冰冷、濕黏，脈搏快而弱，呼吸快而淺，意識混亂或虛弱。',
  'Treat the visible cause (e.g. control any bleeding).': '處理可見的原因（例如控制任何出血）。',
  'Lie the person down; raise their legs if there is no injury (a leg fracture or suspected spinal injury) that raising them would make worse.': '讓對方躺下；如果沒有會因抬高雙腿而加重的損傷（腿部骨折或疑似脊柱損傷），請抬高其雙腿。',
  'Keep them warm, loosen tight clothing, give nothing to eat or drink.': '為其保暖，松開緊身衣物，不要給其吃喝任何東西。',
  'Call the emergency number.': '撥打緊急電話。',
  'Burns and scalds': '燒傷和燙傷',
  'Cool with cool (not ice-cold) running water for 20 minutes, starting as soon as possible — still worth doing up to about 3 hours after the burn.': '用涼的（不是冰冷的）流水沖洗 20 分鐘，越早開始越好，即使在燒傷後約 3 小時內也仍值得這樣做。',
  'Remove jewellery and clothing near the burn unless it is stuck to the skin.': '取下燒傷部位附近的首飾和衣物，除非它們粘在皮膚上。',
  'Cover loosely with cling film (not wrapped tightly around a limb) or a clean, non-fluffy dressing.': '用保鮮膜（不要緊緊纏繞肢體）或乾淨、不掉毛的敷料松松地覆蓋。',
  'Chemical burn: flush continuously with plenty of water.': '化學燒傷：用大量清水持續沖洗。',
  'See a doctor for: a burn larger than the person’s palm; on the face, hands, feet, genitals or a major joint; any blistering burn in a baby or young child; or any electrical or chemical burn.': '出現以下情況請就醫：燒傷面積大於患者手掌；位於面部、手、腳、生殖器或主要關節；嬰幼兒任何起水皰的燒傷；或任何電燒傷或化學燒傷。',
  'No ice, butter, toothpaste, creams or oils.': '不要用冰、黃油、牙膏、藥膏或油。',
  'Do not burst blisters.': '不要弄破水皰。',
  'Heat exhaustion and heat stroke': '熱衰竭與中暑',
  'Heat stroke — confusion, agitation, drowsiness, collapse, hot skin that has STOPPED sweating, seizures: this is a medical emergency. Call for help and start cooling immediately.': '中暑：意識混亂、煩躁、嗜睡、昏倒、皮膚發燙且已停止出汗、抽搐，這是醫療急症。請呼救並立即開始降溫。',
  'Whole-body cold-water immersion (up to the neck) is the fastest method if available. If not: pour or soak with cold water and fan the person, with ice packs at the neck, armpits and groin.': '如有條件，全身浸入冷水（至頸部）是最快的方法。否則：向對方澆冷水或用冷水浸濕，並扇風，同時在頸部、腋窩和腹股溝放置冰袋。',
  'Do not give anything to drink if the person is confused or not fully alert.': '如果對方意識混亂或不完全清醒，不要給其任何飲品。',
  'Heat exhaustion (milder — heavy sweating, tiredness, headache, nausea, still alert): move to shade, cool the skin, sip water or an oral rehydration/sports drink.': '熱衰竭（較輕：大量出汗、疲倦、頭痛、惡心，但仍清醒）：移到陰涼處，給皮膚降溫，小口喝水或口服補液鹽 / 運動飲料。',
  'Seizure (fit)': '癲癇發作（抽搐）',
  'Protect them from injury — move hazards away; do not move the person unless they are somewhere dangerous.': '保護其免受傷害：移開危險物品；除非對方處於危險的地方，否則不要移動對方。',
  'Cushion the head; do not restrain them; put nothing in the mouth.': '墊住頭部；不要約束對方；不要往口中放任何東西。',
  'Time the seizure.': '給發作計時。',
  'Once the jerking stops, place them in the recovery position (above).': '抽搐停止後，讓其採取復甦姿勢（見上文）。',
  'Call the emergency number if: it lasts longer than 5 minutes, it repeats, it is their first ever seizure, they are injured, in water, pregnant, diabetic, or not waking up afterwards.': '出現以下情況請撥打緊急電話：持續超過 5 分鐘、反復發作、這是其第一次發作、對方受傷、在水中、懷孕、有糖尿病，或事後沒有醒來。',
  'Febrile seizures in young children: same basic first aid — never put the child in a cold bath or undress them to bring a fever down.': '幼兒熱性驚厥：基本急救相同，切勿把孩子放進冷水浴或脫光其衣服來降溫。',
  'Head or neck injury, road crash': '頭部或頸部受傷、車禍',
  'Do not move the person unless they are in immediate danger. Keep the head and neck as still as possible.': '除非對方處於直接危險中，否則不要移動。盡量保持頭部和頸部不動。',
  'A motorcycle helmet: leave it on unless you need to remove it to clear the airway or because they are not breathing.': '機車頭盔：除非需要摘下以開啟氣道或因對方沒有呼吸，否則請保持戴著。',
  'Get to hospital for: repeated vomiting, increasing drowsiness or confusion, a worsening or persistent severe headache, a seizure, clear or blood-stained fluid from the nose or ears, or unequal pupil size.': '出現以下情況請去醫院：反復嘔吐、越來越嗜睡或意識混亂、加重或持續的劇烈頭痛、抽搐、鼻或耳流出清亮或帶血的液體，或瞳孔大小不等。',
  'Heart attack': '心臟病發作',
  'Call the emergency number — do not delay this to find aspirin or for any other reason.': '撥打緊急電話，不要為了找阿斯匹靈或任何其他原因而耽擱。',
  'Help the person sit down and rest in a comfortable position.': '幫助對方坐下，並以舒適的姿勢休息。',
  'If they are not allergic to aspirin, have no bleeding disorder, and have not already taken a full dose: have them chew an aspirin while waiting for help (chew a dose in the 150–500 mg range — 300 mg is standard in the UK, 162–325 mg in the US).': '如果對方對阿斯匹靈不過敏、沒有出血性疾病且尚未服過完整劑量：在等待救援時讓其嚼服一片阿斯匹靈（嚼服 150–500 毫克範圍內的一個劑量，英國標準為 300 毫克，美國為 162–325 毫克）。',
  'Stroke — FAST': '中風：FAST',
  'F — Face: has one side dropped?': 'F（面部）：是否有一側下垂？',
  'A — Arms: can they raise both, or does one drift down?': 'A（手臂）：能否同時抬起雙臂，還是有一側下垂？',
  'S — Speech: is it slurred, or can they not speak?': 'S（言語）：是否含糊不清，或無法說話？',
  'T — Time: if any of these, call the emergency number immediately and note the exact time symptoms started — treatment is time-critical.': 'T（時間）：只要出現其中任何一項，請立即撥打緊急電話，並記下症狀開始的確切時間，治療對時間要求很高。',
  '(Some guidance uses "BE FAST", adding Balance and Eyes — a strokes affecting balance or vision can be missed by the classic FAST test alone.)': '（有些指南使用「BE FAST」，增加了平衡（Balance）和眼睛（Eyes），影響平衡或視力的中風，僅用經典的 FAST 測試可能被漏掉。）',
  'Give nothing by mouth — food, drink or medicine — until swallowing has been medically checked.': '在經醫學檢查確認吞咽功能之前，不要經口給予任何東西，包括食物、飲品或藥物。',
  'Low blood sugar (hypoglycaemia)': '低血糖',
  'Conscious and able to swallow: give 15–20 g of fast-acting sugar — glucose tablets, a sugary (not diet) drink, or sweets.': '神志清醒且能吞咽：給予 15–20 克速效糖，如葡萄糖片、含糖（非無糖）飲料或糖果。',
  'Recheck after 10–15 minutes and repeat if still low; once recovered, follow with a slower-acting snack.': '10–15 分鐘後再次檢測，如仍偏低則重復；恢復後，再吃一些吸收較慢的零食。',
  'Drowsy, confused or unconscious: give nothing by mouth (choking risk), put them in the recovery position, and call the emergency number. Give glucagon if one is available and you are trained to use it.': '嗜睡、意識混亂或昏迷：不要經口給予任何東西（有窒息風險），讓其採取復甦姿勢，並撥打緊急電話。如有升糖素且您受過使用培訓，請予以注射。',
  'When a child’s fever needs same-day care': '兒童發燒何時需要當天就醫',
  'Under 3 months old with a temperature of 38°C (100.4°F) or higher: same-day medical assessment, even if the baby seems otherwise well.': '3 個月以下嬰兒體溫達到 38°C（100.4°F）或更高：當天做醫療評估，即使嬰兒看起來其他方面良好。',
  '3–6 months old with a temperature of 39°C (102.2°F) or higher: get medical advice the same day.': '3–6 個月嬰兒體溫達到 39°C（102.2°F）或更高：當天尋求醫療建議。',
  'A child’s appearance and behaviour matter as much as the exact number — treat any of the red-flag signs below as urgent regardless of the reading on the thermometer.': '孩子的外觀和行為與具體數字同樣重要，無論體溫計讀數如何，出現下列任何危險訊號都應視為緊急。',
  'Red flags in a baby or child — get emergency care now': '嬰幼兒的危險訊號：立即獲取急救',
  'Does not respond normally, is very hard to wake, or is floppy.': '沒有正常反應、很難叫醒或軟綿綿。',
  'Blue, grey, very pale or blotchy skin or lips.': '皮膚或嘴唇發紫、發灰、非常蒼白或有斑塊。',
  'Struggling to breathe — grunting, sucking in around the ribs, or pauses in breathing.': '呼吸困難：發出呼嚕聲、肋骨周圍凹陷，或呼吸暫停。',
  'A rash that does not fade when a glass is pressed against it.': '用玻璃杯按壓後不褪色的皮疹。',
  'A fit or seizure.': '抽搐或癲癇發作。',
  'Signs of dehydration: sunken eyes, no tears, dry mouth, very few wet nappies, a sunken soft spot.': '脫水跡象：眼窩凹陷、沒有眼淚、口乾、濕尿布很少、囟門凹陷。',
  'A bulging soft spot (fontanelle), a stiff neck, or a high-pitched, weak or continuous cry.': '囟門隆起、頸部僵硬，或哭聲尖銳、微弱或持續不停。',
  'Diarrhoea, vomiting & dehydration': '腹瀉、嘔吐與脫水',
  'Give oral rehydration solution (ORS) in small, frequent sips. Keep breastfeeding or feeding as normal.': '少量多次地給予口服補液鹽（ORS）。繼續母乳餵養或正常餵食。',
  'No ORS packet available: 6 level teaspoons of sugar and half a level teaspoon of salt, dissolved in 1 litre of clean water — measure the salt carefully, too much can be harmful.': '沒有 ORS 包：6 平茶匙糖和半平茶匙鹽，溶於 1 升乾淨的水中，請仔細量鹽，過多可能有害。',
  'Zinc supplementation, where advised: 10 mg/day under 6 months, 20 mg/day over 6 months, for 10–14 days.': '如醫囑補鋅：6 個月以下每天 10 毫克，6 個月以上每天 20 毫克，持續 10–14 天。',
  'Seek urgent care if the child cannot keep fluids down, passes little or no urine, or shows any of the red-flag signs above.': '如果孩子無法保持攝入液體、排尿很少或沒有，或出現上述任何危險訊號，請立即就醫。',
  'Do not give anti-diarrhoea medicine such as loperamide to a child under 12 without a doctor’s advice, and never to a child who is unwell, dehydrated, or has bloody diarrhoea.': '未經醫生建議，不要給 12 歲以下兒童服用洛派丁胺等止瀉藥，對身體不適、脫水或有血性腹瀉的兒童更不能使用。',
  'Giving a child paracetamol or ibuprofen': '給兒童服用乙醯胺酚或布洛芬',
  'Dose strictly by your child’s weight, following the pack or a doctor/pharmacist’s instructions.': '嚴格按孩子的體重給藥，並遵循藥品包裝或醫生 / 藥劑師的說明。',
  'Do not give ibuprofen to a baby under 6 months, unless a doctor has said to (some guidance allows it from 3 months if the baby weighs at least 5 kg — check the product).': '6 個月以下嬰兒不要服用布洛芬，除非醫生說可以（有些指南允許體重至少 5 公斤的嬰兒從 3 個月起使用，請查看產品說明）。',
  'Never give aspirin to anyone under 19 unless a doctor specifically prescribes it — the risk is Reye’s syndrome.': '除非醫生明確開具，否則不要給 19 歲以下的任何人服用阿斯匹靈，風險是瑞氏綜合徵。',
  'If dengue is a possibility: paracetamol only — never ibuprofen or aspirin, because of bleeding risk.': '如果可能是登革熱：只用乙醯胺酚，絕不能用布洛芬或阿斯匹靈，因為有出血風險。',
  'Dengue warning signs': '登革熱警示症狀',
  'Watch especially as a fever comes down (usually 24–48 hours after it breaks, around days 3–7 of illness) for: severe stomach pain, repeated vomiting (3 or more times in 24 hours), bleeding gums or nose, blood in vomit or stool, extreme tiredness, restlessness or irritability, rapid breathing, cold or clammy skin.': '退燒時（通常是退熱後 24–48 小時，約在發病第 3–7 天）尤其要留意：劇烈胃痛、反復嘔吐（24 小時內 3 次或以上）、牙齦或鼻出血、嘔吐物或大便帶血、極度疲倦、煩躁不安或易怒、呼吸急促、皮膚冰冷或濕黏。',
  'Any one of these means urgent medical care now.': '出現其中任何一項，都意味著需要立即就醫。',
  'While waiting: paracetamol only, and keep the person drinking fluids.': '等待期間：只用乙醯胺酚，並讓對方持續喝水。',
  'Babies and young children are at extra risk of severe dengue.': '嬰幼兒患重症登革熱的風險更高。',
  'A child swallows something poisonous': '孩子吞下了有毒的東西',
  'Do not make them vomit.': '不要催吐。',
  'Call the emergency number, or Thailand’s Ramathibodi Poison Center (1367, 24/7), and bring the container or packaging with you.': '撥打緊急電話，或泰國 Ramathibodi 中毒中心（1367，全天 24 小時），並帶上容器或包裝。',
  'A swallowed button battery is an emergency: go straight to hospital, do not wait.': '吞下紐扣電池屬於緊急情況：直接去醫院，不要等待。',
  'Over 1 year old, and the battery was swallowed within the last 12 hours, and the child can swallow normally: 10 mL (2 teaspoons) of honey by mouth every 10 minutes, up to 6 doses, on the way to hospital — this must never delay getting there.': '1 歲以上，且電池是在過去 12 小時內吞下、孩子能正常吞咽：在去醫院途中，每 10 分鐘口服蜂蜜 10 毫升（2 茶匙），最多 6 次，這絕不能耽誤前往醫院。',
  'Never give honey to a child under 1 year — botulism risk.': '1 歲以下兒童絕不能給蜂蜜，有肉毒桿菌中毒風險。',
  'Water safety for children': '兒童水上安全',
  'Constant, within-arm’s-reach supervision by one sober adult with no other task, whenever a child is in, on or near any water — pool, sea, river, even a bath.': '只要孩子在任何水域（泳池、海、河，甚至浴缸）中、水上或附近，就必須由一名清醒、沒有其他事務的成人持續、在伸手可及的範圍內看護。',
  'A properly fitted, approved child life jacket on boats or in open water.': '乘船或在開闊水域時，穿戴合身且經認證的兒童救生衣。',
  'Drowning is fast and silent, not splashy — it can happen in seconds with no cry for help.': '溺水又快又無聲，不會水花四濺，幾秒鐘內就可能發生，且沒有呼救聲。',
  'Sun and heat with a baby': '嬰兒的防曬與防熱',
  'Keep babies under 6 months out of direct sun — shade, an umbrella or the stroller canopy, and light clothing are the main protection.': '6 個月以下嬰兒應避免陽光直射：遮陰、使用傘或嬰兒車遮篷，並穿輕薄衣物是主要的防護措施。',
  'If shade or clothing genuinely is not possible, a small amount of sunscreen on exposed skin such as the face is acceptable under 6 months.': '如果確實無法遮陰或穿衣，6 個月以下嬰兒可在面部等裸露皮膚上少量塗抹防曬霜。',
  'Exclusively breastfed babies under 6 months do not need extra water, even in heat. Formula-fed babies may be given small amounts of cooled boiled water between feeds in hot weather.': '純母乳餵養的 6 個月以下嬰兒即使在炎熱天氣也不需要額外喝水。配方奶餵養的嬰兒在炎熱天氣，兩次餵奶之間可給少量放涼的開水。',
  'Watch for: fewer wet nappies, dark urine, dry mouth, no tears, unusual sleepiness or fussiness, hot/flushed skin — get medical help if these appear.': '請留意：濕尿布減少、尿色變深、口乾、沒有眼淚、異常嗜睡或煩躁、皮膚發熱 / 潮紅，如出現這些情況請就醫。',
  'Mosquito repellent for babies and children': '嬰幼兒驅蚊劑',
  'Under 2 months: no repellent at all — use a mosquito net over the cot or stroller, screened rooms and covering clothing instead.': '2 個月以下：完全不使用驅蚊劑，請改用嬰兒床或嬰兒車上的蚊帳、有紗窗的房間和遮蓋皮膚的衣物。',
  'From 2 months: DEET up to 30% or picaridin are safe and effective (some countries, e.g. Canada, are more conservative and cap DEET at 10% for young children — check local guidance).': '從 2 個月起：濃度最高 30% 的 DEET 或派卡瑞丁是安全且有效的（有些國家如加拿大更為保守，對幼兒把 DEET 限制在 10%，請查看當地指南）。',
  'No oil of lemon eucalyptus (PMD) under 3 years.': '3 歲以下不要使用檸檬桉油（PMD）。',
  'Apply to your own hands first, then to the child’s face, avoiding eyes and mouth — or apply to clothing instead. Avoid the child’s hands.': '先塗在您自己的手上，再塗到孩子的臉上，避開眼睛和嘴巴，或改為塗在衣服上。避開孩子的手。',
  'Snake bite': '蛇咬傷',
  'Move away from the snake. Keep the person calm and lying as still as possible — movement and panic speed venom through the body.': '遠離蛇。讓傷者保持冷靜並盡量平躺不動，活動和恐慌會加速毒液在體內擴散。',
  'Immobilise the bitten limb with a splint or sling. Remove rings, watches and tight clothing before swelling starts.': '用夾板或吊帶固定被咬傷的肢體。在腫脹開始前取下戒指、手錶和緊身衣物。',
  'Get to a hospital that can give antivenom as fast as possible.': '盡快前往能注射抗蛇毒血清的醫院。',
  'If trained in it: a firm pressure bandage over the whole limb (pressure-immobilisation), plus the splint, is the preferred field technique in this region when the snake cannot be identified — but only if you know how, and never at the cost of delaying transport.': '如果受過相關培訓：對整條肢體使用加壓繃帶（加壓固定法），再加上夾板，是本地區在無法辨認蛇種時首選的現場方法，但前提是您懂得操作，且絕不能以延誤轉運為代價。',
  'Paracetamol, not aspirin or NSAIDs, if pain relief is needed — NSAIDs can worsen bleeding.': '如需止痛，請用乙醯胺酚，不要用阿斯匹靈或非類固醇消炎藥，後者可能加重出血。',
  'Do not cut the wound or try to suck out venom.': '不要切開傷口，也不要試圖把毒液吸出來。',
  'Do not apply a tight tourniquet, ice, an electric shock, alcohol or herbal remedies.': '不要使用緊扎的止血帶，也不要冰敷、電擊、塗酒精或使用草藥偏方。',
  'Do not try to catch or kill the snake — a photo from a safe distance is fine, but never delay travel to identify it.': '不要試圖抓蛇或打死蛇，在安全距離外拍張照片是可以的，但切勿為了辨認它而耽誤送醫。',
  'Washing the wound is fine and even sensible; do not scrub it or apply anything else to it.': '清洗傷口是可以的，甚至是明智的；不要擦洗，也不要在上面塗抹其他東西。',
  'Jellyfish sting (including box jellyfish)': '水母蜇傷（包括箱形水母）',
  'Get out of the water.': '離開水面。',
  'If not breathing normally: start CPR (above) — a box jellyfish sting can be life-threatening within minutes.': '如果呼吸不正常：開始心肺復蘇（見上文），箱形水母蜇傷可在幾分鐘內危及生命。',
  'Pour plenty of vinegar on the sting for at least 30 seconds.': '在蜇傷處大量澆醋至少 30 秒。',
  'Then remove any remaining tentacles with tweezers, a card edge, or a gloved hand — protect yourself from being stung too.': '然後用鑷子、卡片邊緣或戴手套的手取下殘留的觸手，注意保護自己不被蜇到。',
  'Afterwards, for pain: either hot water or a cold pack may help — sources disagree on which is better, so use whichever is available.': '之後針對疼痛：熱水或冷敷袋都可能有幫助，各來源對哪種更好有分歧，用手邊有的即可。',
  'Call the emergency number for severe pain, breathing difficulty, chest discomfort, confusion or collapse. Worse within 30 minutes → urgent care regardless.': '如出現劇烈疼痛、呼吸困難、胸部不適、意識混亂或昏倒，請撥打緊急電話。30 分鐘內加重則無論如何都要緊急就醫。',
  'Do not rub the area.': '不要揉搓該部位。',
  'Do not rinse with fresh water — it can trigger more stings.': '不要用淡水沖洗，否則會引發更多刺細胞放毒。',
  'No alcohol, and no urine.': '不要使用酒精，也不要使用尿液。',
  'Stingray, stonefish or lionfish spine injury': '魟魚、石魚或獅子魚的刺傷',
  'Immerse the wound in water as hot as can be comfortably tolerated without scalding (around 45°C) for roughly 20–90 minutes, or until the pain is controlled.': '把傷口浸泡在能舒適忍受、不至於燙傷的最熱的水中（約 45°C），大約 20–90 分鐘，或直到疼痛得到控制。',
  'Leave an embedded spine or barb in place — it may be plugging the wound — unless a medical professional tells you to remove it.': '嵌入的刺或倒鈎請留在原處，它可能正堵著傷口，除非醫療人員告訴您取出。',
  'Get medical care afterwards: infection risk, a possible retained fragment, antivenom (stonefish), and tetanus risk are all real.': '之後請就醫：感染風險、可能殘留的碎片、抗蛇毒血清（石魚）和破傷風風險都是真實存在的。',
  'A sea urchin puncture is different — do NOT use the hot-water method. Wash it with soap and water instead, and seek care if a spine has gone into a joint.': '海膽刺傷則不同：不要使用熱水浸泡法。請改用肥皂和水清洗，如果刺扎進了關節，請就醫。',
  'Blue-ringed octopus or cone snail': '藍環章魚或芋螺',
  'Keep the person still and calm.': '讓傷者保持不動並冷靜。',
  'Apply a firm pressure-immobilisation bandage over the site and along the whole limb, then splint it — the same technique used for a dangerous snake bite.': '在傷處並沿整條肢體用加壓固定繃帶，然後上夾板，與處理危險毒蛇咬傷的方法相同。',
  'Call the emergency number and get to a hospital without waiting for symptoms to appear.': '撥打緊急電話並前往醫院，不要等症狀出現。',
  'Be ready to give rescue breaths or CPR — the venom can paralyse breathing for several hours, with no antivenom for either animal, and resuscitation must continue until professional help takes over.': '做好進行人工呼吸或心肺復蘇的準備：毒液可能使呼吸麻痹數小時，這兩種動物都沒有抗毒血清，復蘇必須持續到專業人員接手。',
  'Both animals are present in Thai waters (Gulf of Thailand and Andaman Sea); real encounters are rare, since both favour deeper water than most swimmers use, but the risk is severe enough to know this before it happens. Hot water does NOT help this sting (unlike a fish spine) — the toxin is heat-stable.': '這兩種動物在泰國水域（泰國灣和安達曼海）都有；真正遇到的情況很少，因為它們都偏好比大多數游泳者所用水域更深的海水，但風險嚴重，值得在發生之前就瞭解。熱水對這種蜇傷沒有幫助（與魚刺不同），毒素耐熱。',
  'Animal bite, scratch or lick on broken skin (rabies risk)': '動物咬傷、抓傷或舔到破損皮膚（有狂犬病風險）',
  'Wash the wound thoroughly with soap and running water for at least 15 minutes (up to 20 minutes per Thailand-specific guidance) immediately.': '立即用肥皂和流動的水徹底沖洗傷口至少 15 分鐘（按泰國的專門指南最多 20 分鐘）。',
  'Apply an antiseptic (povidone-iodine or alcohol) if you have it.': '如有消毒劑（聚維酮碘或酒精），請塗抹。',
  'Get to a clinic or hospital THE SAME DAY for rabies post-exposure treatment — do not wait to see if the animal seems sick. Vaccine (and immunoglobulin, where indicated) is available at provincial and most district hospitals in Thailand.': '請當天前往診所或醫院接受狂犬病暴露後治療，不要等著看動物是否生病。在泰國，省級和大多數縣級醫院都有疫苗（以及在需要時的免疫球蛋白）。',
  'Vaccinated before the trip: you still need booster doses after a real exposure — say so at the clinic; you will need fewer doses and no immunoglobulin.': '出行前已接種疫苗：真正暴露後仍需要加強針，請在診所說明這一點；您需要的劑量更少，也不需要免疫球蛋白。',
  'Dogs, cats, monkeys and bats can all carry rabies across Thailand, Vietnam, Cambodia and Laos. A lick on broken skin is treated the same as a bite or scratch.': '在泰國、越南、柬埔寨和寮國，狗、貓、猴子和蝙蝠都可能攜帶狂犬病毒。舔到破損皮膚與咬傷或抓傷的處理方式相同。',
  'Caught in a rip current': '被捲入離岸流',
  'Do not try to swim straight back to shore against it — you will exhaust yourself.': '不要試圖逆流直接游回岸邊，那只會使您筋疲力盡。',
  'Stay calm, float or tread water, and raise an arm and call out to signal for help.': '保持冷靜，漂浮或踩水，舉起一隻手臂並呼喊以求救。',
  'Swim parallel to the shore to escape the current, or let it carry you out until it weakens (usually just past the breaking waves) and then swim back at an angle.': '平行於海岸游動以脫離水流，或讓水流帶您出去，直到它減弱（通常剛過碎浪區），然後斜向游回。',
  'A red flag means do not swim. Thailand’s south-west monsoon (roughly May–October) brings rough seas and dangerous rip currents, especially on Andaman (west) coast beaches — ferries and speedboats, including those serving the Trat islands, are sometimes suspended in rough weather.': '紅旗表示禁止游泳。泰國西南季風（大約 5 月至 10 月）會帶來洶湧的海浪和危險的離岸流，尤其是在安達曼（西側）海岸的海灘，渡輪和快艇（包括前往達叻諸島的班次）在惡劣天氣時有時會停運。',
  'Lightning': '雷電',
  'Hearing thunder or seeing lightning nearby: get indoors into a substantial building, or into a hard-topped (metal-roof) vehicle with the windows up.': '聽到雷聲或看到附近有閃電：請進入堅固的建築物內，或進入有硬頂（金屬車頂）且車窗已關閉的車輛中。',
  'Get out of the water and off the beach at once — do not shelter under a beach pavilion, umbrella or open-sided shelter.': '立即離開水面和海灘，不要在海灘涼亭、遮陽傘或四面敞開的遮蔽處躲避。',
  'Wait at least 30 minutes after the last thunderclap before going back outside.': '最後一聲雷響後至少等待 30 分鐘再外出。',
  'A lightning-strike victim carries no electrical charge — it is safe to touch them immediately and start CPR if they are not breathing.': '雷擊受害者身上不帶電，可以立即觸碰，如果沒有呼吸，請立即開始心肺復蘇。',
  'Calling for help in Thailand — beyond the main number': '在泰國求助：主號碼之外',
  '1669 (medical emergency/ambulance) is free from any phone, works nationwide 24 hours, and operators can usually handle basic English — say "English" as soon as the call connects. Response is markedly slower on islands and in rural areas than in Bangkok.': '1669（醫療急救 / 救護車）從任何手機撥打都免費，全國 24 小時可用，接線員通常能應對基本英語，接通後請立即說「English」。海島和鄉村地區的響應明顯比曼谷慢。',
  '191 is police, 199 is fire — both free and 24 hours.': '191 是警察，199 是消防，均免費，24 小時可用。',
  '1155 is the Tourist Police: a free, 24-hour hotline specifically staffed for English-speaking travellers — a good parallel or backup call, though not a replacement for 1669 in a medical emergency.': '1155 是旅遊警察：一條免費的 24 小時熱線，專門配備了會說英語的人員，可作為並行或備用的求助電話，但在醫療急症時不能代替 1669。',
  '1367 is the Ramathibodi Poison Center’s 24/7 consultation hotline.': '1367 是 Ramathibodi 中毒中心的 24 小時咨詢熱線。',
  '1199 is the Marine Department’s 24-hour hotline for water incidents (boats, ferries, accidents at sea).': '1199 是海事局的 24 小時熱線，處理水上事件（船隻、渡輪、海上事故）。',
  'This is Thailand-specific detail underneath the country’s own main emergency number, which this app already shows at the top of the SOS and hospital screens for whichever country you are in.': '這是泰國專屬的細節，位於該國自己的主要緊急電話之下，本應用已在「緊急求助」和醫院頁面頂部顯示您所在國家的主要緊急電話。',
  'Insurance and getting evacuated': '保險與緊急後送',
  'Comprehensive travel insurance covering medical treatment AND emergency evacuation (including from remote islands) is not optional here — do not assume your home healthcare system covers this.': '涵蓋醫療和緊急後送（包括從偏遠海島後送）的全面旅行保險在這裡不是可選項，不要假定您本國的醫療體系會承擔這些。',
  'Foreigners are charged for all medical treatment; there is no reciprocal free-healthcare arrangement.': '外國人所有醫療都要收費；沒有互惠的免費醫療安排。',
  'Private hospitals — the fastest, highest-standard option — commonly want a deposit or a formal insurer "guarantee of payment" before non-emergency treatment. Even with insurance, you may be billed as self-pay until that guarantee arrives, which can take 24–72 hours or more.': '私立醫院是最快、標準最高的選擇，通常在非緊急治療前要求預付押金或保險公司正式的「付款擔保」。即使有保險，在擔保到位之前（可能需要 24–72 小時甚至更久），您也可能被按自費計費。',
  'Call your insurer’s assistance line as early as possible — ideally before admission, not after.': '請盡早聯絡保險公司的援助熱線，最好在入院之前，而不是之後。',
  'Malaria, dengue and Japanese encephalitis risk': '瘧疾、登革熱和日本腦炎風險',
  'Malaria in Thailand is concentrated in remote, forested border areas (with Cambodia, Myanmar and Malaysia) — the tourist islands themselves are low or negligible risk, and routine antimalarial tablets are generally not needed for an island or beach trip.': '泰國的瘧疾集中在偏遠的森林邊境地區（與柬埔寨、緬甸和馬來西亞交界處），旅遊海島本身風險很低或可忽略，海島或海灘之旅一般不需要常規服用抗瘧藥。',
  'Dengue is different: it is endemic across Thailand, Vietnam, Cambodia and Laos, including all the islands, year-round with a rainy-season peak. There is no vaccine relied on for casual travel — bite avoidance (repellent, covering clothing, screens) is the real prevention.': '登革熱則不同：它在泰國、越南、柬埔寨和寮國（包括所有海島）全年流行，雨季達到高峰。目前沒有可供一般旅行依賴的疫苗，避免蚊蟲叮咬（驅蚊劑、遮蓋皮膚的衣物、紗窗）才是真正的預防辦法。',
  'Japanese encephalitis occurs countrywide outside Bangkok, peaking seasonally (roughly May–October), and is weighted toward rural, rice-farming areas. Vaccination is mainly advised for longer stays (a month or more) or higher-risk itineraries.': '日本腦炎在曼谷以外的全國範圍內發生，有季節性高峰（大約 5 月至 10 月），多集中在鄉村稻作地區。主要建議長期停留（一個月或以上）或風險較高的行程接種疫苗。',
  'Anyone trekking into remote forest near an international border should get individual pre-trip travel-clinic advice regardless of the above.': '無論上述情況如何，任何前往國際邊境附近偏遠森林徒步的人，都應在出發前向旅行門診獲取個人化的建議。',
};
